I am a Ph.D. Candidate in Political Science at the [University of California, Los Angeles](https://polisci.ucla.edu). My research sits at the intersection of American local politics, voting behavior, and public opinion. My dissertation — *The Supply and Demand of Municipal Policy in a Polarized Era* — examines how partisan polarization shapes the politics of city governance.

My work has been published in *Urban Affairs Review* and has been supported by fellowships from the Institute for Human Studies, the UCLA Division of Graduate Education, and the UCLA Institute to Study Hate, among others.

I am on the job market for 2026–2027.
